            "notes": "**Round five!**\n\nThis is where things get exciting again, because it once again depends a bit on how the game is going and how your team is doing.\n\nIf I used [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4) as my second power, it's definitely time for [Supply Surge](item_35d75d9e-66b7-426a-b92d-9dfd72ee5fbb)!\n\nIf you already have [Supply Surge](item_35d75d9e-66b7-426a-b92d-9dfd72ee5fbb), then [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4) is a good option for more healing on the fifth round, or if you have a strong second support, [Distortion](item_5557e2f2-02df-4eac-8128-0c23b71183b1) to further boost the team. \n\n[Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1) can also be a good choice, but with so much cooldown reduction, we should be slippery enough by now to be able to easily evade even dive heroes.\n\nSince we build a lot of cooldown anyway, [First Responder](item_30a5c70f-e0b5-489a-96ae-900f34c3823d) can also be very useful if you notice that a teammate is being picked a lot, in order to bring a teammate back as often as possible.\n\nWhen it comes to items, we continue to focus on a good mix of cooldown reduction, Weapon Power, and Attack Speed.\n\nI usually want the 20% cooldown reduction on the fifth turn, so [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) and [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) are pretty much always included. Instead of Martian, a combination of [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f) and [Ironclad Exhaust Ports](item_2d085fa5-ace6-4fab-9323-b7a06268bcd0) is also possible, of course; it depends on the cash and the situation.",
