            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-08T12:53:02.260309+00:00",
            "notes": "**Seventh Round!**\n\nThings get wild again here, because with [The Whambulance](item_67e91029-d0fc-4c9d-9733-ec7e1cc064a9), the build now becomes a hybrid version.\n\nIt's important to note that Whambulance's healing isn't the mainstay here, as in a full AP build. Rather, it's a combination of Weapon Power and Ability Power.\n\nThe choice of AP items depends heavily on what's going on.\n\n[Iridescent Iris](item_b7fb28ef-ce82-416b-8693-01c274f8df4e) is very nice, as it gives us cooldown reduction and overhealth if we need to ult in a critical situation.\n\n[Angelic Acrobatics](item_baad85fc-3da5-43af-ad9d-f17885f59aa5) is very useful when we're constantly being harassed by Genji, Winston, Dva, etc.\n\n[Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) fits very well into the build, as it gives us weapon power and ability power. Since we'll always have the stacks, the item gives us 25 HP, 10 WP, and 25 AP.\n\n[Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) is simply a very good survival item overall, and it also provides AP.\n\nIf necessary, [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) can also be replaced with a second AP item this round.\n\nWith the items selected on the left, our total, with active stacks, would be:\n50 Weapon Power\n45 Ability Power\n20 Attack Speed\n20 Cooldown Reduction\n453 Health\n\n\n**BUT!\n\nThis build can also be played without AP. Instead of Whambulance, you can use [Serenity](item_c6e1c072-ff50-467e-b59f-9506baea10c1), [Distortion](item_5557e2f2-02df-4eac-8128-0c23b71183b1), or [First Responder](item_30a5c70f-e0b5-489a-96ae-900f34c3823d) and fill the last item slot with a Survival or Weapon Damage item. \n\nDue to the already high cooldown reduction in this build, [First Responder](item_30a5c70f-e0b5-489a-96ae-900f34c3823d) is particularly well-suited for rezzing as often as possible**",
